# /sdlc-doctor

Run `./scripts/sdlc doctor` (on Windows PowerShell or cmd: `.\scripts\sdlc.cmd doctor`) and tell the person what it found. It only looks; it changes nothing.

- Every line says `ok` and it ends with "toolchain ready": say so in one sentence, name the Python and Node versions it printed, and suggest `/sdlc-setup` next.
- Any line that is not `ok`: list each problem with the fix the tool printed next to it (an install command or a link), in the order it printed them.
  Do not install anything yourself and do not edit any file: the person decides what goes on their machine.
- Do not guess. If the output is unclear, show the relevant lines exactly as printed.
